~< set ns.n = ns.n + 1 >~
\section*{<< ns.n >>. Notices and Emergency Contact}
Landlord notices shall be delivered to \textbf{<< notices.landlord_address | default(landlord.address, true) | latex >>}. Tenant's notice address is \textbf{<< notices.tenant_address | default("", true) | latex >>}. Rent shall be paid by << notices.payment_method | default("", true) | latex >>.

\textbf{Landlord contact:} << notices.landlord_name | default(landlord.name, true) | latex >>; << notices.landlord_phone | default(company.phone, true) | latex >>; << notices.landlord_email | default(company.email, true) | latex >>.

~< if emergency_contact.name or emergency_contact.phone >~
\textbf{Emergency contact:} << emergency_contact.name | default(landlord.name, true) | latex >>; << emergency_contact.phone | default(company.phone, true) | latex >>. This contact may coordinate emergency access and repairs but may not change the Tenant's rights under this Agreement.
~< endif >~

~< if landlord.name or tenant or draft >~
~< set ns.n = ns.n + 1 >~
\section*{<< ns.n >>. Signatures}
The parties have executed this Agreement as of the date first written above. The parties shall sign or initial each attached disclosure and addendum actually delivered with this Agreement. No statement in this section substitutes for delivery of a required notice or disclosure.

